 "poem": "Farewell, my dear boy! When haply today\nYour father sends his letters home away;\nAnd leaves us now alone to dedicate\nOur souls for love and deeds of dedication.\nA man's faith may seem more true than today,\nIn that while life is in the grave location,\nHis hopes shall be all but lost on decay,\nAnd folly, with its frail winged shadow lay.\nThough falling weeps, though yet not ever starvation,\nBut shall we turn day by day separated\nFrom our young spirit who fascination\nThe things we feel? - No: a day will able",
